    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an E15 error code and wont start. i looked at the manual but i'm not sure what to do first. how do i check the leak sensor and how can i dry out the bottom of the machine if there's water stuck down there?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, find the small bag on the front control panel where it connects to the bottom rack. Pull it gently out, and you'll see the bright yellow sensor labeled \"Leak Sensor\". Try plugging it into another outlet that works, or temporarily reconnect it to a different outlet (it won't shock you if it does get shocked). If it cycles through a few lights, the door isn't leaking, and the leak sensor isn't the problem. If it stays on, dry out the bottom of the dishwasher with a towel and wait for it to cycle through completely, which may take an hour or more.",
      "source": "target",
