    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "a metal hammer?? that sounds like it might break the sensor or the plastic tray. is there a way to get the water out without potentially damaging the machine? also i tried the shut off button thing and nothing happened, it's still just sitting there with the error code. why would water even get into that bottom tray in the first place if the door is closed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. If there's still water in the bottom tray after shutting off the dishwasher and patting it dry, let it drip out. To not damage the water sensor, I don't recommend using a long stick or hammer to tap out the water. More for safety sake than practically speaking since you could just break the trap underneath.\n\nIf water is still in the bottom tray after that, carefully position a small drain pan or saucer under the dishwasher and then tilt it slightly. The water should drain out as your machine is draining the dishwasher itself. Just be careful to point the drainage away from any expensive flooring.\n\nAs to why there's water in the bottom tray at all, it could be from a number of things. First, you would need to check whether the dishwasher door hangs off the bottom on that side or if the door gasket (seal) around the door is bad and won't close on that side. You can check both of these things with paper and force the door gently to the left and right sides. Also, check around the door to see everything fits and doesn't rub against the rim.\n\nAnother thing to remember is the scanner and the probes at the front line above the height control. Just be careful that it fits against the side on",
      "source": "target",
      "gen_token_ids": [
        11756,
        10384,
        395,
        290,
        38441,
        13,
        1843,
